+### 2026-10-27
+- **Board, Priorities and Dump are on the page structure, so every page but Plan is built one way** (the next PR the component-structure spike planned; no behavior change). Each route reads its data and renders one container — `BoardPage`, `PrioritiesPage`, `DumpPage` — which owns the page's state and writes, renders its own header, and hands the writes down through a page context: `BoardScreen` and `PrioritiesScreen` are gone and `DumpScreen` is renamed. The biggest gain is on Priorities, where the quadrant cell and the card each went from 9 props to 2 and track and Done no longer pass through four components on desktop. The Priorities and Dump routes shape their data with pure adapters (`toPrioritiesPageProps`, `toDumpPageProps`, the no-plan week and the feed unwrapping), which the scenarios reuse on raw fixtures; the matrix's grouping and its "tracked" check became shared helpers, all with unit tests.
+- **The docs follow**: `baseline.md` and AGENTS.md name Plan as the one page left (it moves with Phase 2's Plan week), the Design Console README covers the new inert contexts and the scenarios' adapters, and the tracker's Step 10 is down to writing up the Q9 comparison and archiving the spike, plus the config-driven modals. Verified: format, lint, typecheck, knip, the unit and integration suites, all 26 e2e tests, a click-through of every context handler on the three live pages (16/16) and a browser check of the Board's tabs.
